__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Policy: EVERYTHING under output/ is committed. The Stage 1 reference snapshot,
# the full GA scored population, and the complete per-candidate gate4 output --
# every alignment, tree, distance matrix, model file and IQ-TREE checkpoint. Only
# two classes remain ignored: third-party tool binaries, and the two top-level
# pipeline logs that are rewritten wholesale on every run. Both are below.
#
# Measured cost (2026-10-13), in the order the files were added:
#   * The gate4 tree output looked like 498 MB over 740 files. It is not: 53.6%
#     of those files are byte-identical across candidates and Git stores content
#     once (231 MB of distinct blobs), and the FASTA/.mldist/.phy text packs at
#     3.6x. With the Stage 1 snapshot's 74 MB of JSON (which packs 10.6x to
#     7 MB), the measured pack growth for 685 files and 535 MB of raw output was
#     ~2 MB -- Git's delta compression across the near-identical alignments of
#     each species pair beat a per-file estimate by an order of magnitude.
#   * tree.ckp.gz is the exception and the only real cost here: 60 files, 36.9 MB,
#     already gzipped so Git cannot compress or delta them at all. Budget the
#     full 36.9 MB. They were briefly excluded as solver scratch, which was
#     wrong: alongside the resume state they carry the consensus tree,
#     contree_rfdist and the UFBoot and model blocks.
# Still far inside every GitHub limit (100 MB per file -- largest here is
# 27.5 MB; 2 GB per push; 5 GB per repository). Re-measure with:
#     git count-objects -vH
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# External tool binaries: 38 MB of downloadable archives plus their extracted trees.
# The pin is recorded by tools/CHECKSUMS.sha256 and tools/VERSIONS.txt, which ARE
# tracked -- committing the artifacts themselves would bloat the repo to no purpose.
tools/dist/
tools/mafft-win/
tools/iqtree-3.1.3-Windows/
tools/_download_meta.json

# The two top-level pipeline logs. Unlike every other artifact here they are
# rewritten wholesale on every run, so tracking them makes each rerun a large
# diff against the previous machine's timings rather than a result change.
# Nothing in them is secret -- the paths they embed are the project directory,
# with no username or home path -- and every figure that matters from them
# (record counts, isolate and triplet totals, pool sizes, per-phylogroup
# runtimes) is reproduced in README.md. Drop these two lines if you want them.
# Note this pattern is depth-1 only: the 60 per-candidate IQ-TREE tree.log files
# under output/ga_search/.../ are deliberately NOT matched and ARE tracked.
output/ortho_pipeline.log
output/ortho_phylogeny.log

# run_main.sh archives output/ to a sibling directory outside the repo.
# Adding the pattern here covers the case where someone runs it from inside the repo.
_pipeline_archive/
